@startuml
title SRM RFQ Lifecycle - State Machine
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #334155
  ArrowColor #475569
}

[*] --> Draft : Buyer creates RFQ
Draft --> ValidationFailed : Required data invalid
ValidationFailed --> Draft : Buyer corrects data
Draft --> PendingApproval : Submit for configured approval
Draft --> Published : Publish without approval
when policy permits

state "Pending Approval" as PendingApproval
PendingApproval --> Approved : Required approvers approve
PendingApproval --> ChangesRequested : Send back
PendingApproval --> Rejected : Reject
ChangesRequested --> Draft : Buyer revises and resubmits
Rejected --> [*] : Close rejected RFQ

Approved --> Published : Publish RFQ
Published --> OpenForResponse : Invitations issued
OpenForResponse --> Extended : Authorized deadline extension
Extended --> OpenForResponse : New deadline becomes effective
OpenForResponse --> Evaluation : Deadline reached
or authorized early close
OpenForResponse --> Cancelled : Cancel with reason
Published --> Cancelled : Cancel before response window
Evaluation --> Negotiation : Evaluation complete
and negotiation required
Evaluation --> AwardPending : No negotiation required
Negotiation --> AwardPending : Final commercial position recorded
AwardPending --> Awarded : Award approved and recorded
AwardPending --> Evaluation : Returned for re-evaluation
Awarded --> Closed : Notifications and closure checks complete
Evaluation --> Cancelled : Cancel with authorization
Negotiation --> Cancelled : Cancel with authorization
Cancelled --> [*]
Closed --> [*]

note right of OpenForResponse
Supplier responses remain confidential.
Deadline lock, extension permissions,
minimum response rules and exception
handling are policy-controlled.
end note
@enduml
